  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 316 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nThe frontal boundary, anchored over northern Kansas will lift \nnorth as a warm front Wednesday into southern Nebraska. By \nafternoon, a lead shortwave will initiate convection along the \nfront range of Colorado. Southwesterly winds aloft will lift \nthis activity into the forecast area Wednesday evening into the \novernight hours. The front will remain stalled across central \nand southern Nebraska Thursday with a secondary shortwave \nleading to convective development over the central Rockies. Once\nagain, southwesterly flow aloft will carry activity into the \narea Thursday night into Friday morning. Beyond Friday, there \nwill be continued threat for showers and thunderstorms into the \nweekend as low pressure aloft slowly lifts across the northern \nRockies. After highs in the 80s Friday, temperatures will be \nseasonal this weekend with highs in the 70s.",
